  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 214 PM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\n\nSaturday night through Thursday Assessment...very high (>80%) \nconfidence on above normal temperatures.\n\nThe upper level ridge retrogrades briefly into the Plains for the \nsecond half of the holiday weekend but will then push back east for \nthe middle of next week. Thus after a brief reprieve from the heat \nSunday/Monday, heat and humidity will surge back into the area \nTuesday/Wednesday with heat indices approaching 100.\n\nBy late next week the overall flow pattern aloft de-amplifies \nslightly. This will allow temperatures to be closer to but still \nabove normal.\n\nAny rain chances the first half of next week are low (10-25%) and \nare confined to areas along/north of I-80. Thus there will be many \nhours of dry weather.\n\nThe models are attempting to bring a front into the area Tuesday \nnight into Wednesday with the front progged to stall and wash out \nacross the area. The proximity of the front has the model consensus \ngiving slightly higher rain chances (30-50%) for late Tuesday night.\n\nOnce the front stalls and washes out across the area, its remnants \nwould then provide the focus for rain chances the remainder of the \nweek. However, even with a near daily chance of rain, the rain \nchances remain low (20-30%) with the better forcing remaining across \nthe northern Plains and upper Midwest.",
